# --- Database ---
# Works with any Postgres-protocol endpoint: local docker, Neon, Supabase, RDS.
# We use `postgres-js` (the standard Postgres wire protocol) for both dev and prod.
#
# ⚠ THIS IS A PLACEHOLDER TEMPLATE, NOT A DESCRIPTION OF THE REAL
# ENVIRONMENT. As of 2026-10-08 the real setup is TWO SEPARATE Neon
# PROJECTS: one for production (configured in Vercel), one for local
# development (configured in `.env` and `.env.local`). The localhost
# value below is never what actually runs.
#
# Do not infer deployed state from this file. To check what is really
# configured, look at `.env`, `.env.local`, `.vercel/project.json` and
# the migrations in `drizzle/`. A session once told the user "the prod
# database doesn't exist yet" based on line 4 of this file. It was
# wrong. See `docs/drift/2026-10-08-production-is-live.md`.
#
# Migrations: local `pnpm db:migrate` hits the DEV project only —
# production migrations are applied by Vercel's `prebuild` when the
# commit reaches `main`.
POSTGRES_URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/nextep

# --- App ---
# These two are the canonical site origin. Precedence is
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL → BASE_URL → http://localhost:3000, resolved in
# lib/site.ts and consumed by app/sitemap.ts, app/robots.ts, the OG/canonical
# tags, and share links. Set BOTH to the real origin in production, using
# the www form: https://www.nexstepper.com
BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
NODE_ENV=development

# --- Site verification ---
# Optional. When set, Next.js emits
# <meta name="google-site-verification" content="..."> on every page.
# Leave it EMPTY for local dev and CI — an empty tag reads as a failed
# verification to whoever debugs it later.
#
# This is the HTML-method proof of domain ownership. Prefer the DNS TXT
# method for production: it needs no deploy, covers the apex + www + any
# subdomain at once, and survives refactors. Set this only as a second
# proof, or for environments where you cannot edit DNS.
#
# CAUTION: robots.txt and sitemap.xml are prerendered STATIC, so the ORIGIN
# they bake in is frozen at build time — NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL must be
# correct when the build runs. The verification tag itself lives in the
# root layout, and every page renders dynamically (the layout awaits
# getUser()), so this token is read at runtime and appears without a
# redeploy. Set this var in the Vercel project's environment, not just
# in your shell.
GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=

# --- Auth (Better Auth) ---
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=replace_me_with_openssl_rand_base64_32
BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- Google Sign-In (OPTIONAL) ---
# Nexstepper works on email + password alone. This is opt-in: set BOTH
# vars and /sign-in + /sign-up render "Continue with Google"; set
# neither and nothing changes. A half-set pair (ID but no secret)
# disables the provider rather than crashing at runtime.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
#
# Setup in Google Cloud Console → Google Auth Platform:
#   1. Create or select a project
#   2. Branding — app name, support email, homepage, privacy policy URL,
#      authorized domain `nexstepper.com`
#   3. Audience — External
#   4. Data Access — add `openid`, `email`, `profile` ONLY.
#      Basic identity scopes keep this app exempt from Google's
#      100-user test cap and its "unverified app" warning screen.
#      Adding Gmail or Drive scopes opts you into Google verification
#      and a security review instead.
#   5. Credentials → Create Credentials → OAuth client ID →
#      Application type: **Web application**
#   6. Authorized redirect URIs — Google matches these EXACTLY:
#        http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/google
#        https://www.nexstepper.com/api/auth/callback/google
#        https://nexstepper.com/api/auth/callback/google
#      Register BOTH production hosts: Vercel 308-redirects the apex
#      to `www.`, so missing one produces a `redirect_uri_mismatch`
#      in production only (see the trustedOrigins note in lib/auth.ts).
#
# Not a paid service. Google charges nothing for OAuth sign-in at any
# user volume. See docs/drift/2026-10-08-production-is-live.md.

# --- Stripe ---
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_replace_me
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_replace_me
# Create matching products in Stripe (price IDs go here).
STRIPE_PRICE_ID_FREE=
STRIPE_PRICE_ID_PRO=

# --- AI (Vercel AI Gateway) ---
# The Gateway is the recommended way to talk to model providers from
# this app. One key routes to Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, Mistral,
# DeepSeek, and 200+ other models — with 0% markup, automatic
# cross-provider failover, and built-in spend/latency observability
# in the Vercel dashboard.
#
# Get a free key (no card, $5/mo free credit on the free tier):
#   https://vercel.com/dashboard → AI Gateway → API Keys
#
# In production on Vercel, prefer the OIDC token over a static key:
#   set VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN (auto-provisioned) and leave
#   AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY unset.
AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=

# Legacy direct-provider keys (optional). Only needed if you bypass
# the Gateway for a specific call. Most code paths now use the
# Gateway and don't touch these.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-replace_me
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-replace_me

# --- Email (Resend) ---
RESEND_API_KEY=re_replace_me
RESEND_FROM_ADDRESS=Nexstepper <hi@nexstepper.com>

# --- Observability ---
# Sentry
SENTRY_DSN=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
# Build-time Sentry config (only needed in CI / Vercel deploy for
# sourcemap upload + release tagging; local dev without these is fine).
SENTRY_ORG=
SENTRY_PROJECT=
SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=

# POSTHOG_KEY is the server-side secret (posthog-node, AI observability).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY is the client-side token (posthog-js init in
# instrumentation-client.ts). They share the same project but are
# different keys — see PostHog project settings for both values.
POSTHOG_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=
# Host config is split too: POSTHOG_HOST is for server-side SDK calls,
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST is what the browser sends events to. They
# default to the same US endpoint if both are left blank.
POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# --- Realtime (Liveblocks) ---
LIVEBLOCKS_SECRET_KEY=sk_dev_replace_me
NEXT_PUBLIC_LIVEBLOCKS_PUBLIC_KEY=pk_dev_replace_me

# --- Background jobs (Inngest) ---
INNGEST_EVENT_KEY=
INNGEST_SIGNING_KEY=